    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d897">

                <pb facs="0838" n="748" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg748"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860d.00/6</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-02-08T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 8,
                                1918, 7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>531. Consul, Helsingfors, telegraphs urgently for recognition of Finland. He says
                    will gain sympathy of Norway-Sweden-Denmark League of which Finland will be
                    member. What are your views as to action and as to stability of present Finnish
                    government? This <pb facs="0839" n="749" xml:id="pg749"/> Government appreciates
                    thoroughly the historical, political, and economic considerations which would
                    prompt a desire for recognition on the part of Finland. Answer promptly and
                    fully. In this connection you may assure Finnish Chargé d’Affaires if occasion
                    offers that the desire of the United States to assist Finland with food supplies
                    is only limited by the urgent and vital needs of our allies and of our own
                    forces in France.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
